    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite score of 75.30. Despite facing a formidable arm in Woo (xERA 3.42), **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a dynamic platoon advantage that elevates his floor significantly. **Kyle Tucker** (68.96) and **Josh Jung** (65.46) follow closely as our top-tier plays; **Josh Jung** is a particularly high-upside start, as his base projection was boosted by a +8% BvP historical edge against Wacha and a +5% favorable wind condition. Meanwhile, **Andy Pages** (63.73) remains a high-efficiency start in the two-hole, capitalizing on the favorable matchup against Keller and neutral platoon splits.\n\nOur most difficult decision centered on the bottom of the order, where **Liam Hicks** (57.76) and **Miguel Vargas** (58.80) landed just inside our \"Strong\" start threshold. **Liam Hicks** earns his spot at C1 primarily due to the lineup-order boost (+10%) from leading off, offsetting a lower base projection. The bench was relatively quiet due to the off-days for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**, along with the continued injury absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**. **Sam Antonacci** (44.84) and **Coby Mayo** (41.80) were the primary candidates for removal, both lingering in the marginal territory. **Coby Mayo** was nearly benched in favor of a deeper reserve like **Heliot Ramos** or **Jacob Wilson**, but his +16% park adjustment kept him in the lineup over bench options that lacked the same situational environment. Managers should monitor **Liam Hicks** closely, as any late lineup shuffling could diminish his lead-off value and drop him below the efficiency floor.",
